From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:32:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Carry form-control state on ScenePart

A checkbox is a box with a tick in it, and a radio is a circle with a
dot. Both are drawn, so a consumer reading only geometry cannot tell a
checked control from an unchecked one with a decorative glyph nearby,
or either of them from a rounded border.

The DOM is the only thing that knows, and it is right there at paint
time, so the state rides on the part rather than being reconstructed
downstream.
---
 src/lib.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 5669436..8a7d6dc 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -205,6 +205,13 @@ pub enum ScenePart {
     TextDecoration,
     /// A list item's bullet or number.
     Marker,
+    /// A checkbox, with its live checked state. Carried on the part
+    /// rather than left to the backend to work out, because the DOM is
+    /// the only thing that knows it and a backend drawing a control
+    /// has to agree with `:checked`.
+    Checkbox { checked: bool },
+    /// A radio button, likewise.
+    Radio { checked: bool },
 }

 pub trait PaintScene: RenderContext {
